            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use the walking-only region and the addition rule to find 6 favourable students out of 30.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "The number who walk but use neither bus nor train is $15-8-3=4$. Thus 23 students use bus or train. Using the addition rule for counts:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n|B\\cup T|&=30-3-4=23\\\\\n|B\\cap T|&=17+16-23=10\\\\\n|B\\cap T\\cap\\overline{W}|&=10-4=6\\\\\nP(B\\cap T\\cap\\overline{W})&=\\frac{6}{30}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
